---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/comparison-caption-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Comparison caption study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of comparison captions for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="comparison-caption-study">
    <div class="shell comparison-caption-study-intro">
      <a class="comparison-caption-study-back" href="/prototypes/comparison-label-study/">← Comparison label study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should the work be identified?</h1>
      <p class="comparison-caption-study-lede">Three treatments for the small caption under a comparison: useful context, without turning the interaction into a dashboard.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell comparison-caption-study-grid">
      <article class="caption-option"><p class="caption-option-name"><span>A</span> Quiet line</p><div class="caption-demo caption-demo--quiet">Drag to compare · Dundrum Inn, Dundrum</div><p>A single muted line keeps the focus on the images.</p></article>
      <article class="caption-option"><p class="caption-option-name"><span>B</span> Split caption</p><div class="caption-demo caption-demo--split"><span>Drag to compare</span><strong>Dundrum Inn</strong><small>Dundrum</small></div><p>Separates instruction, subject, and place for faster scanning.</p></article>
      <article class="caption-option"><p class="caption-option-name"><span>C</span> Framed detail</p><div class="caption-demo caption-demo--framed"><strong>Dundrum Inn</strong><span>Independent concept · Dundrum</span></div><p>Gives the subject more presence with a small rule and stronger type.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
